# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-8), L §6.1: a `same` line joins kinds, things and movements, never two rows of a state or
# reading input; L §8.3 LOAD-SAME "same <p> = <q>: <what p is> and <what q is>" (a row of an input on either side).
# A version's line between two rows of one model's inputs is refused. Inside one model the figure is a def that reads
# both inputs (MIGRATION.md § 2.1 → 2.2).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input fee_bank[m in months]: money PLN
input fee_broker[m in months]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  fee_bank[2026-03] = 10.00 PLN "bank"
  fee_broker[2026-03] = 10.00 PLN "broker"
  same fee_bank[2026-03] = fee_broker[2026-03]

ask q: fee_bank[2026-03]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-SAME same fee_bank[2026-03] = fee_broker[2026-03]: a row of an input and a row of an input (m.tally:18)
